---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { production } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Cookies & Website Storage | EFIops"
  description="Cookies and similar technologies used by the EFIops website."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Website storage</p>
      <h1>Cookies and similar technologies.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container legal">
    {!production && (
      <p class="preview-note">
        Review notice: the final host and any additional services must be checked before launch.
      </p>
    )}
    <section>
      <h2>The website as built</h2>
      <p>
        The website does not set cookies or use local storage for analytics, advertising or
        personalisation. Fonts, the logo and illustrations are served with the website. Optional
        analytics, advertising pixels, booking widgets and external media embeds are disabled.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Your enquiry</h2>
      <p>
        The form uses a random request identifier to help prevent duplicate submissions. It is held
        in the page while it is open, rather than stored in a cookie or local storage. After an
        accepted enquiry, a temporary acceptance timestamp in session storage allows the
        confirmation page to show the received message. That timestamp contains no enquiry details
        and is removed when the confirmation page loads.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Dashboard sign-in</h2>
      <p>
        The admin dashboard uses essential authentication cookies to keep its authorised owner
        signed in. These cookies are HttpOnly, are restricted to dashboard API requests and use
        Secure protection on HTTPS. They are cleared on sign-out. This storage is used for access
        security, not advertising or analytics.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>If optional services change</h2>
      <p>
        Before enabling optional tracking or embedded services, EFIops must review their storage,
        purposes and provider arrangements, update this notice and provide appropriate controls.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Questions about information</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/privacy/">Read how EFIops handles your information.</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
